From 7b36ed12849d20c27b15c160e2845f1cebdb43a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: g1-door <g1-door@local>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:32:51 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] door: record why each episode ended and write evaluation
 videos only for chosen envs (when the state recorder is on,
 _check_termination keeps per env the reason bits of the last end (stage
 overtime, completion or episode limit, base termination, 4 m from the door,
 upper-body joint overspeed, door at door_hold_open_angle_deg), the stage, and
 the fastest upper-body joint and its speed, carried over until the next end
 because the recorder writes the state after the reset; reset_buf is an
 integer buffer, so it is turned into a mask first;
 simulator.config.render_env_ids writes videos only for those envs while the
 camera still covers every env, since Isaac Lab 3.0 needs one camera per env;
 judgments unchanged, default off = unchanged) (11-02)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
